<section>
  <div class="container">
    <div class="prose" style="max-width:720px">
      <h2>Martyn's Law (Terrorism (Protection of Premises) Act 2025)</h2>
      <p><strong>Who it affects:</strong> Schools, academies, community centres, sports clubs and any venue that can reasonably expect 200+ people at once.<br>
      <strong>Key date:</strong> Enforceable from spring 2027 (24-month implementation period from April 2025 commencement; Home Office published final statutory guidance April 2026).<br>
      <strong>What's required:</strong> Standard-tier venues need documented procedures for an attack (invacuation, lockdown, evacuation) and trained staff &mdash; not physical security infrastructure.<br>
      <a href="/blog/martyns-law-schools-north-west/">Read our full guide &rarr;</a></p>

      <h2>Awaab's Law Phase 2</h2>
      <p><strong>Who it affects:</strong> Housing associations, local authorities and registered social housing providers.<br>
      <strong>Key date:</strong> 30 November 2026.<br>
      <strong>What's required:</strong> Fixed response deadlines extend beyond damp and mould to excess cold/heat, falls, structural collapse, fire/explosions, electrical hazards, and hygiene/food safety. Asbestos and carbon monoxide follow in 2027.<br>
      <a href="/blog/awaabs-law-phase-2-housing-associations/">Read our full guide &rarr;</a></p>

      <h2>Crime and Policing Act 2026 &mdash; safeguarding changes</h2>
      <p><strong>Who it affects:</strong> Schools and nurseries.<br>
      <strong>Key date:</strong> From 1 September 2026 (2026/27 academic year).<br>
      <strong>What's required:</strong> Removes the long-standing supervision exemption from the definition of regulated activity, affecting how schools manage visitors and site access.</p>

      <h2>Building Safety Act 2022 / Building Safety Regulator oversight</h2>
      <p><strong>Who it affects:</strong> Higher-risk buildings and, increasingly, wider commercial and public-sector estates as BSR oversight extends.<br>
      <strong>What's changing:</strong> Updated fire door standards and a continuing shift from paper-based to digital compliance record-keeping.</p>

      <blockquote>Not sure which of these apply to your site? <a href="/contact/">Book a free 30-minute consultation</a> and we'll walk through what's relevant to you.<br><br>This page is general guidance, not legal advice, and reflects our understanding of the regulatory position at the time of writing. For a definitive view, consult the relevant statutory guidance or a qualified adviser.</blockquote>
    </div>
